      "summary": "Natural death after a short illness; exact disease debated",
      "detail": "Edward IV died suddenly at Westminster on 9 April 1483 after a short illness. The precise diagnosis is debated (pneumonia, malaria, typhoid, apoplexy or even poisoning have been suggested), but the death itself was of natural causes; he was only 40.",
